{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"Module 09 — Administrative Application Security\nWhitelist → Blacklist → Sandbox → Patch → WAF","x":-560,"y":-2330,"width":400,"height":60,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b1","type":"text","text":"Whitelisting (LO01a)\nTrust-centric · allow approved only · deny by default\nAdvantages: stops malware, zero-day, bandwidth loss,\nlicensing lawsuits, reduces attack surface + BYOD risk\nImplement via SRP (Active Directory): 4 rules = Path ·\nHash · Certificate (not default) · Internet Zone (.msi only)\nAppLocker: exes, MSIs, DLLs · folder-path default rules ·\nedition-limited rule collections","x":-1650,"y":-2120,"width":370,"height":210,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b2","type":"text","text":"Blacklisting (LO01b)\nThreat-centric · allow by default · deny known-bad\nUsed by AV, spam filters, IDS/IPS\nCons: never comprehensive · no zero-day defense\nManageEngine Endpoint Central: Block Executable\n(path/hash) + Prohibit Software (auto-uninstall)\nWindows PUA: Set-MpPreference -PUAProtection 1\nGroup Policy: Turn off Windows Installer (Always)\nRegistry: DisallowRun strings 1,2,3 = exe names","x":-1650,"y":-1830,"width":370,"height":230,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b3","type":"text","text":"Sandboxing (LO02a)\nSealed container for untrusted/untested 3rd-party code\nLimitation: not robust vs kernel-targeting malware\nIsolation-based (no outside access) vs Rule-based\n(resources per policies)\nExamples: browsers (JS sandboxed), PDF/Office macros,\nmobile apps, UAC (low/med/high integrity)\nChrome --site-per-process · Firefox\nsecurity.sandbox.content.level · Acrobat Protected Mode","x":-1650,"y":-1520,"width":370,"height":230,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b4","type":"text","text":"Sandbox Tools (LO02b)\nWindows Sandbox (vitualization needed) · Firejail\n(SUID + namespaces + seccomp-bpf: firejail firefox)\nSandboxie Plus (Sophos) · BufferZone · SHADE ·\nShadow Defender (reboot discards) · Docker · Cuckoo ·\nDeepArmor · Turbo.net\nWDAG (Edge): SLAT + 4 cores + Win10 Ent; install via\nEnable-WindowsOptionalFeature; standalone vs enterprise\n(trusted *.microsoft.com / neutral bing.com)","x":-1650,"y":-1210,"width":370,"height":230,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b5","type":"text","text":"Patch Management (LO03)\nMonitor + deploy new/missing patches (hackers exploit\npatch-disclosed vulns quickly)\nFlow: scan → central download → select per-client →\ntest → deploy if pass\nFeatures: 3rd-party patching, network scan, patch-status\ndashboard (patched+malicious / unrecognized / unknown /\ncompliance), test-first, group staging (avoid congestion)\nSolarWinds Patch Manager (WSUS, SCCM); PDQ Deploy,\nShavlik, Kaseya, Flexera, HP Touchpoint, Ivanti, Syxsense, Itarian","x":-1650,"y":-900,"width":370,"height":240,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b6","type":"text","text":"WAF (LO04a/b)\nLayer-7 rule-filter ahead of web app; firewall/IDS-IPS fail there\nTypes: Network/hardware · Host/software · Cloud-hosted\nDeployments: reverse proxy · L2 bridge · out-of-band ·\nserver resident · internet-hosted cloud\nBenefits: cookie encryption/signature, CSRF, URL-encryption\nanti-tampering, data-validation, PCI/HIPAA/GDPR\nLimits: can't read DB commands, needs session mgmt for\nanti-automation, false positives, not NGFW\nURLScan (IIS, reject by verb/ext/encoding); NAXSI\n(positive model) · Cloudflare · Wallarm (API Top 10) ·\nFortiWeb · AppWall (Slowloris, brute-force) · WebKnight","x":-1150,"y":-2120,"width":440,"height":260,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"b7","type":"text","text":"Why it matters\nAdministrative app security = controlling what runs, how it\nruns isolated, what gets patched, and what traffic a web\napp accepts. Whitelist + sandbox shrink attack surface;\npatch mgmt closes the disclosed-vuln window; WAF catches\nL7 attacks network defenses miss.","x":-1150,"y":-1780,"width":440,"height":170,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b8","type":"text","text":"Flow\nResponsibilities → whitelist/blacklist decision → choose\ncontrols (SRP/AppLocker/Endpoint Central/Registry)\n→ sandbox untrusted code → enforce patch cadence →\ndeploy WAF for web apps\nPolicy drives all 4: whitelist & blacklist = the trust model;\nsandbox = the isolation model; patch = the time model;\nWAF = the traffic model","x":-1150,"y":-1530,"width":440,"height":200,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"end","type":"text","text":"Module Summary points\n5 admin practices = whitelisting, blacklisting, sandboxing,\npatch management, application-level firewall (WAF)\nImplement: SRP/AppLocker (domain) · Endpoint Central\n+ PUA + Registry (blacklist/tools) · Windows Sandbox,\nFirejail, Sandboxie, WDAG (sandbox) · SolarWinds Patch\nManager + others (patch) · URLScan + commercial WAFs\nOnly material in the PDFs; no invented #TODO facts","x":440,"y":-1900,"width":440,"height":200,"color":"5"}
	],
